  "instructions": [
    "In a large mixing bowl, whisk together eggs, sugar, and a pinch of salt until well combined.",
    "Add in flour, baking powder, and a splash of red wine, whisking until smooth.",
    "Heat a large skillet over medium heat, add a pat of salted butter and swirl to coat.",
    "Using a piping bag, pipe the egg mixture into agave leaves, filling to about 3/4 full.",
    "Fry the egg eclairs in the skillet until golden brown and crunchy, about 3-4 minutes per side.",
    "Remove from heat and let cool on a wire rack.",
    "Dust with confectioners' sugar and garnish with fresh thyme and rosemary.",
    "For the glaze, whisk together granulated sugar and a splash of red wine until smooth.",
    "Drizzle the glaze over the cooled egg eclairs and sprinkle with crushed almond meal.",
    "Serve immediately and enjoy!",
    "Store any leftovers in an airtight container in the refrigerator for up to 3 days.",
    "Reheat in the oven or microwave before serving.",
    "Note: Best served fresh, but still delicious after reheating."
  ],
